{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790367064,"nonce":"XxCYwrzQQfwSb8IkqorjOEWDj8M=","title":"Lua: the string library reads an embedder's buffers in place","message":"An embedder's byte buffer (caribou's Buffer) crossing into Lua should stay itself, not be copied into a Lua string, and Lua should read it where it lies: caribou issue 75a6b13205476df16024d828dccdd11a23250fcb0953df2c98f037ce16df07cf.\n\nzyntax_embed::foreign::Foreign gains bytes(object) -\u003e Option\u003c(ptr, len)\u003e, default none, with a $Foreign$bytes_len symbol and foreign::bytes_of for natives. zyntax_lua's string.len, string.sub, string.byte, string.unpack and # accept a foreign object that is a buffer: a new Param::Bytes kind keeps a statically typed string on the typed implementation, and sends anything else to its $any form, which reads a string's or a buffer's bytes through natives that take the value. A foreign object that is not a buffer is refused as before (string expected, got userdata). tests/foreign.rs.","files":null}]}